  "notes": "Root cause fixed: `store.update()` was never implemented in MemoryStore despite task 169-004 claiming it was added. Tests failed with `TypeError: store.update is not a function`. Fixes applied: (1) Added `update(id, fields, changedBy)` method to MemoryStore with whitelist-driven column patch (content/title/summary/metadata/status/priority/decay_exempt), automatic FTS5 *_norm mirror columns refresh for text fields, updated_at bump, and entry_history rows. (2) Fixed backfill-stub-entries.mjs: entry ID lookup now tries `mem-sprint-{N}` first then falls back to `mem-{N}` (live DB uses the latter pattern); default archiveDir changed from `.brain/archive` to `.brain` so path resolves to `.brain/sprints/sprint-N.md` (correct live path); stub detection now handles `stub_flag === null` (live entries without explicit flag) — updates content if archive exists, otherwise just clears stub_flag with `archive_unavailable: true`; idempotent skip only for `stub_flag === false`. (3) Also fixed `throw new Error()` violations in `insertRelation` (introduced by task 169-003) — imported DeckentError from ./errors.js and replaced both violations with `DeckentError('DECKENT_E068/E069', ...)` to pass error-handling-unification test. Live DB backfill executed: sprint-159 content updated from `.brain/sprints/sprint-159.md` (2083 chars) + stub_flag cleared; sprint-160 and sprint-161 had no archive file — metadata.stub_flag set to false with archive_unavailable:true. GO/NO_GO criteria met: all 3 entries have `length(content) > 100` and `json_extract(metadata, '$.stub_flag') = 0`. 4/4 TDD tests PASS. tsc --noEmit clean. vitest: 16497 pass / 1 fail (pre-existing alert-emitter) / 66 skip.",
